; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Sierpinski Carpet
; CATEGORY: Fractals
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     recursion, squares, FILLED, color gradient
; SUMMARY:  Weaves the Sierpinski carpet out of eight smaller carpets around an empty middle.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Cut a square into a 3 by 3 grid and throw away the middle. Do
;   the same to each of the eight squares that are left, and again,
;   and again. Only the tiniest squares are actually painted, and
;   their color slides from blue at the bottom left to orange at the
;   top right.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change the depth (last line) to 1, 2, 3 or 5.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * recursion with two FOR loops inside it
;   * skipping one case with IF
;   * computing an RGB color from the turtle's position
;   * why painting only the smallest pieces avoids overlaps
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Also skip the four corners. Which fractal do you get?
;   * Paint every tiny square a random color with RANDOM 256.
;   * Depth 5 makes 32768 squares. How long does it take?
; ============================================================

; TILE paints one solid square with its bottom left corner at (x, y).
to tile :x :y :size
  ; Mix the color from the position: x and y run from -243 to 243,
  ; so (x + 243) / 486 goes from 0 to 1 across the carpet.
  localmake "a (:x + 243) / 486
  localmake "b (:y + 243) / 486
  localmake "mix (:a + :b) / 2
  penup setxy :x :y setheading 0
  filled (list 40 + 210 * :mix 80 + 60 * :a 230 - 200 * :mix) [
    repeat 4 [forward :size right 90]
  ]
end

; CARPET splits the square into nine and recurses into eight of them.
to carpet :x :y :size :depth
  if :depth = 0 [tile :x :y :size stop]
  localmake "third :size / 3
  for [row 0 2] [
    for [col 0 2] [
      ; The middle square, row 1 column 1, is the hole.
      if not and :row = 1 :col = 1 [
        carpet :x + :col * :third :y + :row * :third :third :depth - 1
      ]
    ]
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [250 246 236]
; 486 is 2 times 3 to the power 5, so every tiny square is a whole
; number of steps wide at depth 4 and 5.
carpet -243 -243 486 4
